ral Arts\nCollege of Life & Physical Sciences\nCollege of Public Service\nAcademic Programs\nHonors College\nRegistrar\nLibraries & Media Center\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nCampus Tour\nFinancial Aid\nScholarships\nTuition & Costs\nFAQ\u2019s\nStudent Life\nActivities\nHousing\nBookstore\nThe Meter\nLeadership & Organizations\nService Learning\nOffice of Technology Services (OTS)\nWeb Services\nResearch\nInstitutional Research\nResearch Centers of Excellence\nAthletics\nMake a Gift\nMYTSU Login\nComputer\nScience\nCollege of Engineering\nComputer Science\nAbout\nDegrees\nFaculty\nApply\nExplore Colleges & Schools\nCollege of Engineering\nComputer Science\nAbout\nDegrees\nFaculty\nApply\nBSCS Program Accredited by ABET/CAC\nApply Now\nBachelor of Science (B.S.)\nThe Department of Computer Science offers an exciting B.S. degree with a broad-based knowledge in various contemporary computer science fields such as computer architecture and organization, software systems, algorithm design and analysis, computer programming, database management systems, computer networks and data communication, cybersecurity, and artificial intelligence.\nThe B.S. degree program in Computer Science is accredited by the Computing Accreditation Commission of ABET.\nView CS program objectives and outcomes>>\nConcentrations for the Bachelor of Science in Computer Science\nData Science\nCybersecurity and Networking\nBioinformatics\nSpring 2026\nFaculty Tutoring Schedule\nFaculty Office Hours and Advisement Schedule\nUndergraduate Catalog\nGraduation Requirements\nScholarship Applications (due January 15, 2025)\nGraduate Assistant Application Form\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Resources\nMaster\u2019s Degree (M.S.)\nThe Department of Computer Science offers a M.S. degree in Computer Science. The program provides college graduates an opportunity to enhance their careers and work on cutting-edge areas of computer science. The program offers two high-demand concentrations:\nConcentrations for the Master of Science in Computer Science\nData Science\nCybersecurity and Networking\nHPC and Bioinformatics\nPhD Degree\nThe Department of Computer Science offers a PhD in Engineering and Computational Sciences Program in partnership with the College of Engineering.\nConcentrations and Specialties for the PhD in Engineering and Computational Sciences\nComputational Sciences Concentration\nData Science Specialty\nCybersecurity and Networking Specialty\nHPC and Bioinformatics Specialty\nEngineering Systems Concentration\nCareers\nThe Department of Computer Science has strong relations with IT Industry and Government Agencies. Our graduates are employed in the following areas:\nSoftware Engineering\nApplication Programming\nSystem Programming\nComputer Architectures\nArtificial Intelligence and Robotics\nDNA and Cloud Computing\nDistributed and Parallel Systems\nComputer Communications, Networks, and Security\nBioinformatics\nSome of the companies and agencies that hire our students are listed as:\nIBM\nHCA\nGoogle\nMicrosoft\nAmazon\nBank of America\nOracle\nLockheed Martin\nNorthrop Grumman\nRaytheon\nEvents & Announcements\nStay up to date with what's going on around campus\nJoin Our Newsletter\nSubscribe to receive the latest Tennessee State University news, events, and important updates.\nEmail\nThis field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged.\nEmail\nSubmit\nBy subscribing you agree to with our Privacy Policy\nAlumni\nAlumni\nTSU Foundation\nSupport\nHomecoming\nEstate Planning\nAdmissions\nAdmissions\nTuition & Costs\nFinancial Aid\nTransfer\nCampus Tour\nAbout\nAbout\nCampus\nPresident\nBoard of Trustees\nNondiscrimination Statement\nUniversity Calendar\nResearch\nSMART AI Center\nCampus Map\nTitle III\nContact\n3500 John A Merritt Blvd\nNashville, TN 37209\nTel: (615) 963-5000\nHelp Desk Ticket\nHelp Desk Phone: 615-963-7777\n\u00a9 Tennessee State University. All Rights Reserved.\n|\nJLB - Nashville Web Design & 